# CI/CD y Cloud Run — {{ repo_name }}

Setup **de una sola vez** para que la pipeline
({% if ci_gl %}`.gitlab-ci.yml`{% else %}`.github/workflows/ci.yml` + `deploy.yml`{% endif %})
construya con Cloud Build y despliegue a Cloud Run **sin claves JSON**
(Workload Identity Federation). Ningún secreto, audience, project number ni
email vive en el repo.

```bash
git tag qa-v0.1.0   && git push origin qa-v0.1.0     # tests + govulncheck + Trivy + deploy a QA
git tag prod-v0.1.0 && git push origin prod-v0.1.0   # idem prod
```

```
Internet ─▶ {{ repo_name }} (público, allUsers) ──TLS + ID token──▶ items-service (interno)
            SA {{ repo_name }}-sa                                   run.invoker: {{ repo_name }}-sa
```

## 1. Variables de trabajo

```bash
export PROJECT_ID={{ gcp_project }}
export REGION={{ gcp_region }}
export REPO_NAME={{ artifact_repo }}
export DEPLOYER_SA=ci-deployer                # puede ser el mismo de los micros
export RUNTIME_SA={{ repo_name }}-sa
export POOL_ID=ci-pool
{%- if ci_gl %}
export PROVIDER_ID=gitlab-provider
export REPO_PATH=<grupo>/{{ repo_name }}
{%- else %}
export PROVIDER_ID=github-provider
export REPO_PATH=<owner>/{{ repo_name }}
{%- endif %}
export PROJECT_NUMBER="$(gcloud projects describe "$PROJECT_ID" --format='value(projectNumber)')"
export DEPLOYER_SA_EMAIL="${DEPLOYER_SA}@${PROJECT_ID}.iam.gserviceaccount.com"
```

## 2. Runtime: SA, Artifact Registry, invoker sobre los servicios{% if a_key %}, secreto de API keys{% endif %}

```bash
UPSTREAM_SERVICES="items-service-qa" ./scripts/setup_cloud_run.sh qa
UPSTREAM_SERVICES="items-service"    ./scripts/setup_cloud_run.sh prod
```

Crea `{{ repo_name }}-sa` **sin roles de proyecto**, el repo `{{ artifact_repo }}`
y le da `roles/run.invoker` **sobre cada servicio** listado (no sobre el
proyecto).{% if a_key %} Crea el secreto `{{ repo_name }}-api-keys-<entorno>` (empieza
con `keys: []`) con acceso de lectura solo para ese SA.{% endif %} Volvé a
correrlo después del primer deploy: hace público al gateway (`allUsers`
invoker). Si la organización prohíbe `allUsers` (*domain restricted
sharing*), poné un Load Balancer externo delante (y entonces
`TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=2`).

## 3. Upstreams en `cloudrun.<env>.yaml`

Completá `UPSTREAM_ITEMS_ADDR` (host de Cloud Run del servicio + `:443`):

```bash
gcloud run services describe items-service-qa --region "$REGION" --format='value(status.url)'
# https://items-service-qa-abc123-uc.a.run.app  ->  items-service-qa-abc123-uc.a.run.app:443
```

`UPSTREAM_TLS=true` + `UPSTREAM_AUTH=google-idtoken`: el gateway pide al
servidor de metadata un ID token con audience `https://<host>` (o
`UPSTREAM_<NAME>_AUDIENCE`) y lo manda en cada llamada; Cloud Run lo valida
contra el `run.invoker`. También completá `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` con el
dominio exacto del front de cada entorno.

## 4. Service account deployer

```bash
gcloud iam service-accounts create "$DEPLOYER_SA" --display-name="CI deployer" --project "$PROJECT_ID" || true
for ROLE in roles/cloudbuild.builds.editor roles/storage.admin roles/run.admin; do
  gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding "$PROJECT_ID" \
    --member="serviceAccount:${DEPLOYER_SA_EMAIL}" --role="$ROLE"
done
gcloud iam service-accounts add-iam-policy-binding "${RUNTIME_SA}@${PROJECT_ID}.iam.gserviceaccount.com" \
  --member="serviceAccount:${DEPLOYER_SA_EMAIL}" --role="roles/iam.serviceAccountUser" --project "$PROJECT_ID"
gcloud artifacts repositories add-iam-policy-binding "$REPO_NAME" --location="$REGION" --project "$PROJECT_ID" \
  --member="serviceAccount:${DEPLOYER_SA_EMAIL}" --role="roles/artifactregistry.reader"
```

## 5. Workload Identity Federation

Si ya hay pool/provider para otros repos, sumá este al `attribute-condition`
del provider existente. Desde cero:

```bash
gcloud iam workload-identity-pools create "$POOL_ID" --location=global --project "$PROJECT_ID" || true
{%- if ci_gl %}
gcloud iam workload-identity-pools providers create-oidc "$PROVIDER_ID" \
  --location=global --project "$PROJECT_ID" --workload-identity-pool="$POOL_ID" \
  --issuer-uri="https://gitlab.com" \
  --attribute-mapping="google.subject=assertion.sub,attribute.project_path=assertion.project_path,attribute.ref=assertion.ref" \
  --attribute-condition="assertion.project_path in ['${REPO_PATH}']"
gcloud iam service-accounts add-iam-policy-binding "$DEPLOYER_SA_EMAIL" --project "$PROJECT_ID" \
  --role="roles/iam.workloadIdentityUser" \
  --member="principalSet://iam.googleapis.com/projects/${PROJECT_NUMBER}/locations/global/workloadIdentityPools/${POOL_ID}/attribute.project_path/${REPO_PATH}"
{%- else %}
gcloud iam workload-identity-pools providers create-oidc "$PROVIDER_ID" \
  --location=global --project "$PROJECT_ID" --workload-identity-pool="$POOL_ID" \
  --issuer-uri="https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com" \
  --attribute-mapping="google.subject=assertion.sub,attribute.repository=assertion.repository,attribute.ref=assertion.ref" \
  --attribute-condition="assertion.repository in ['${REPO_PATH}']"
gcloud iam service-accounts add-iam-policy-binding "$DEPLOYER_SA_EMAIL" --project "$PROJECT_ID" \
  --role="roles/iam.workloadIdentityUser" \
  --member="principalSet://iam.googleapis.com/projects/${PROJECT_NUMBER}/locations/global/workloadIdentityPools/${POOL_ID}/attribute.repository/${REPO_PATH}"
{%- endif %}
```

## 6. Variables de la CI y protección de tags
{% if ci_gl %}
Settings > CI/CD > Variables:

| Variable | Valor |
|---|---|
| `GCP_DEPLOYER_SA` | `$DEPLOYER_SA_EMAIL` |
| `GCP_WIF_AUD` | `https://iam.googleapis.com/projects/${PROJECT_NUMBER}/locations/global/workloadIdentityPools/${POOL_ID}/providers/${PROVIDER_ID}` |
| `GCP_PROJECT` | opcional; pisa `{{ gcp_project }}` |

Protected tags: `prod-v*` → Maintainers; `qa-v*` → Developers + Maintainers
(proteger los tags **antes** de marcar variables como *Protected*).
{%- if protos_module %}
Repo de protos (`{{ protos_module }}`): Settings > CI/CD > Job token
permissions → agregar este proyecto a la allowlist.
{%- endif %}
{% else %}
Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions > Variables:

| Variable | Valor |
|---|---|
| `GCP_DEPLOYER_SA` | `$DEPLOYER_SA_EMAIL` |
| `GCP_WIF_PROVIDER` | `projects/${PROJECT_NUMBER}/locations/global/workloadIdentityPools/${POOL_ID}/providers/${PROVIDER_ID}` |
| `GCP_PROJECT` | opcional; pisa `{{ gcp_project }}` |

Environments `qa` y `prod` (en `prod`: solo tags `prod-v*` y *Required
reviewers*) y un tag ruleset sobre `prod-v*`.
{%- if protos_module %}
Secret `PROTOS_TOKEN`: token de solo lectura al repo de protos.
{%- endif %}
{% endif %}
## Qué corre la pipeline

1. `test`: `go mod verify`, gofmt, `go vet`, `go test` (con los tests de
   autorización generados desde `routes.yaml`), `govulncheck`, `go mod vendor`.
2. Imagen (`{% if ci_gl %}build-image{% else %}image{% endif %}`) + Trivy: `docker build` del mismo commit y `vendor/`; falla con
   vulnerabilidades HIGH/CRITICAL que tengan fix.
3. Release (tag): Cloud Build construye y publica en Artifact Registry con el
   mismo Dockerfile y `vendor/`, y `gcloud run services replace`. Recomendado:
   activar el escaneo de Artifact Registry para vigilar la imagen publicada.

## Rollback

```bash
./scripts/rollback.sh qa                 # imágenes y revisiones disponibles
./scripts/rollback.sh prod prod-v0.1.0   # redespliega una imagen existente (pide confirmación)
```
